# Data: never commit the large DMA dumps.
# These are deliberately anchored rather than bare globs. A plain *.csv also matches the
# DIRECTORY src/AisPipeline.Adapters.Csv, because git sets core.ignorecase=true on macOS --
# which silently excluded that whole project until CI failed on a fresh clone.
data/
/*.csv
/*.zip

# .NET
bin/
obj/
*.user
[Dd]ebug/
[Rr]elease/
TestResults/
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal

# OS / editor
.DS_Store
.vs/
.idea/

# Planning notes kept local: they reference context that does not belong in a public repo
ais-pipeline-plan_1.md

# Reference documents are NEVER committed. This repo is public; the source material is not ours
# to redistribute, and some of it carries real commercial data -- vessel names, cargo quantities,
# agent signatures.
#
# Deny everything, allow back only the README that cites it. The previous rule listed *.pdf, which
# silently failed to cover the .webp scans that were actually added, and two real Statements of
# Facts reached a public repository as a result. An extension allow-list is the wrong shape here:
# the rule has to be "nothing, except", or the next unanticipated format walks straight through.
docs/reference/**
!docs/reference/
!docs/reference/**/
!docs/reference/**/README.md
